Q:
Find the following limit using either forms or continuity: lim as x -> infinity of (x^2-4x-sqrt(x))/(1-(x^2-2x)^(1/3))

A:
-infinity

lim as x -> infinity of (x^2-4x-sqrt(x))/(1-(x^2-2x)^(1/3)) ~ lim as x -> infinity of x^2/(-(x^2)^(1/3))

This simplifies further:

lim as x -> infinity of x^2/(-(x^2)^(1/3)) = lim as x -> infinity of x^2/(-x^(2/3)) = lim as x -> infinity of (x^2 · x^(-2/3))/(-1) = lim as x -> infinity of x^(4/3)/(-1)

This is form infinity/-1 which approaches -infinity.

Thus lim as x -> infinity of x^2/(-(x^2)^(1/3)) = -infinity.

